Modifications: standalone includes and integer types; host-endian surface struct;
C bridge and input validation; game-specific FFL workaround omitted.
Coordinate bit scan uses __builtin_clz on the 32-bit operand (not clzl).
Aperture bridge follows GX2_TilingAperture.cpp::retileTexture with bounds checks.

Standalone OpenGL shader translation in decompiler/:
- LatteDecompiler*.cpp/.h, LatteDecompilerEmitGLSLHeader.hpp:
  src/Cafe/HW/Latte/LegacyShaderDecompiler/ (same basenames)
- FetchShader.cpp/.h, LatteConst.h, LatteShaderAssembly.h, LatteShader.h,
  LatteGSCopyShaderParser.cpp: src/Cafe/HW/Latte/Core/ (same basenames)
- registers.h: remaining register definitions from ISA/LatteReg.h
- RegDefines.h and LatteInstructions.h: src/Cafe/HW/Latte/ISA/
- inputs.cpp: Core/LatteShader.cpp::LatteShader_CreatePSInputTable.
Adaptations: standalone includes/types, standard vectors replacing Boost vectors,
OpenGL-only renderer selection, Metal framebuffer-fetch analysis omitted, no Cemu
performance instrumentation or native fetch-shader cache/Vulkan hash, owned fetch
attribute arrays, thread-local pixel input table. StringBuf.h is a new growing
std::string adapter, avoiding the original fixed-buffer formatting limit.
No game shader programs or generated shader text are included.
